<article class="env-definition" id="0ANS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ANS">Definition <span data-tag="0ANS">87.29.1</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a continuous map of topological rings (More on Algebra, Definition <a href="/tag/07E8" data-tag="07E8">15.37.1</a>). We say $B$ is <em>topologically of finite type over</em> $A$ if there exists an $A$-algebra map $A[x_1, \ldots , x_ n] \to B$ whose image is dense in $B$. </p>
